      "summary": "Panko toasted in rendered bacon fat and butter with onion, garlic, orange zest and parsley — a dry, crumbly farofa.",
      "method_md": "**Panko Farofa**<br><br>**Ingredients**\n\t- ¾ cup panko breadcrumbs<br> 40 g bacon, diced<br> ½ tbsp unsalted butter<br> ½ small onion or shallot, diced<br> ½ clove garlic, minced<br> ¼ tsp orange zest<br> ¼ tsp kosher salt<br> Black pepper<br> 2 tsp parsley, chopped\n\t*Optional:* 15 g toasted nuts (almonds or cashews)<br><br>**Method**<br>1. Render bacon on medium heat (\\~5 min).<br>2. Add butter and onion. Cook 3 minutes.<br>3. Add garlic for 30 seconds.<br>4. Add panko and toast 3–4 minutes until golden.<br>5. Stir in orange zest and parsley.<br>6. Texture goal: dry and crumbly.<br>7. Serve warm.",
